      "@id": "x:doc",
      "@type": "Container"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Dysregulation of innate and adaptive serum mediators precedes systemic lupus erythematosus classification and improves prognostic accuracy of autoantibodies",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n1",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Samples were obtained from the DoDSR. Demographic and clinical information, including medication history and American College of Rheumatology (ACR) criteria for SLE classification, were extracted from medical records by study personnel.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n2",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Serum levels of BLyS (R & D Systems, Minneapolis, MN) and a proliferation-inducing ligand (APRIL) (eBioscience/Affymetrix, San Diego, CA) were assessed using enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) per manufacturer's protocol.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n3",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Normalized fluorescence intensity values for an additional 30 immune mediators, including cytokines, chemokines, and soluble TNFR superfamily members (Supplemental Table 2), were determined by xMAP multiplex assays (eBioscience/Affymetrix) [18].",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n4",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The BioPlex 2200® system (Bio-Rad Technologies) was used to simultaneously detect levels of multiple autoantibody specificities within a single serum sample: dsDNA, chromatin, Ro/SSA, La/SSB, Sm, SmRNP, and RNP [7,35].",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n5",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Mixed linear regression models were fitted on normalized FI values of each soluble mediator over time using the lme4 package in R (version 2.15.0). Using mixed models, intercepts were modeled as random effects to account for the initial soluble mediator le",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n6",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "To determine if other forms of immune dysregulation contribute to preclinical SLE pathogenesis, we measured SLE-associated autoantibodies and soluble mediators in samples from 84 individuals collected prior to SLE classification",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n7",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "To better understand the temporal relationship between soluble mediator dysregulation and autoantibody production, we next compared the timing of autoantibody specificity detection and soluble mediator dysregulation as patients moved toward SLE classificat",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n8",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Cases who later developed SLE exhibited increased inflammatory mediators from multiple immune pathways more than 3.5 years pre-classification (Fig. 1 and Table 1).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n9",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Cases moving toward SLE classification gained an average of 0.5 dysregulated mediators per year, compared to only 0.06 in controls (p < 0.001; Fig. 2A and Table 2).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n10",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Of note, multiple TNF superfamily members, including TNFRI, TNFRII, BLyS, and APRIL, were dysregulated only as patients approached SLE classification (Fig. 1 and Table 1).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n11",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The detection of most lupus-associated autoantibody specificities occurred significantly later than the onset of IL-4, IL-5, IL-6, IFN-γ, or MIG dysregulation (Fig. 3 and Table 3).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n12",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Over the entire pre-classification period, random forest models incorporating ANA and anti-Ro/SSA positivity with levels of IL-5, IL-6, and the IFN-γ-induced chemokine, MIG, distinguished future SLE patients with 92% (±1.8%) accuracy, compared to 78% accur",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n13",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "However, ANA negative, IL-5 and IFN-γ high cases (SLE cluster 1) were more likely to develop nephritis (p = 0.008), while cases who were ANA positive were more likely to develop arthritis (p = 0.028) as they transitioned to classified SLE.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n14",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Indeed, these two mediators were elevated in about 20% of future SLE patients at least 6 years prior to disease transition and in approximately 90% of SLE patients by two years after classification.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n15",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Thus, the early elevation of IFN-γ, followed by significant increases in BLyS and APRIL within one year of disease classification when SLE is imminent, supports the model that simultaneous dysregulation of T helper, regulatory, IFN-related, and TNF-related",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n16",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "IL-5 1.38 (1.24 e 1.62) 0.86 (0.64 e 1.26) 4.35E-06",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n17",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Cases moving toward SLE classification gained an average of 0.5 dysregulated mediators per year, compared to only 0.06 in controls (p < 0.001; Fig. 2A and Table 2).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n18",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Mixed linear regression models confirmed that cases had significant longitudinal increases in the levels of these mediators (Table 2), including BLyS (p = 0.008, Fig. 2G) and APRIL (p = 0.013, Fig. 2H), compared to minimal changes in controls during the sa",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n19",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "anti-dsDNA 3.14 (2.13, 4.63) 5.28 (3.56, 7.82) 4.22 (2.85, 6.25) 3.06 (2.11, 4.44) 4.11 (2.80, 6.06)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n20",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Combined IL-6, anti-Ro/SSA, IL-5, ANA, MIG 0.93 (0.87, 0.97) 0.89 (0.77, 0.96) 0.96 (0.90, 0.99) 0.84(0.71, 0.93) 92% ± 1.78%",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n21",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "However, ANA negative, IL-5 and IFN-γ high cases (SLE cluster 1) were more likely to develop nephritis (p = 0.008), while cases who were ANA positive were more likely to develop arthritis (p = 0.028) as they transitioned to classified SLE.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n22",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Future prospective, longitudinal studies of individuals with autoantibody positivity ± immune dysregulation, prior to onset of clinical signs and symptoms, will be necessary to determine which autoimmune disease(s) are associated with particular dysregulat",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n23",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Although the cellular sources of dysregulated soluble mediators in preclinical SLE remain unknown and are the subject of future study",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n24",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Additional, future studies will be required to determine if dysregulation of signaling pathways that leads to aberrant cellular activation and secretion of inflammatory mediators is due to genetic, epigenetic, and/or environmental triggers",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Samples were obtained from the DoDSR. Demographic and clinical information, including medication history and American College of Rheumatology (ACR) criteria for SLE classification, were extracted from medical records by study personnel.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r1",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Serum levels of BLyS (R & D Systems, Minneapolis, MN) and a proliferation-inducing ligand (APRIL) (eBioscience/Affymetrix, San Diego, CA) were assessed using enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) per manufacturer's protocol.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
