      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "IL-5 1.38 (1.24 e 1.62) 0.86 (0.64 e 1.26) 4.35E-06",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r6",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Cases moving toward SLE classification gained an average of 0.5 dysregulated mediators per year, compared to only 0.06 in controls (p < 0.001; Fig. 2A and Table 2).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r7",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Mixed linear regression models confirmed that cases had significant longitudinal increases in the levels of these mediators (Table 2), including BLyS (p = 0.008, Fig. 2G) and APRIL (p = 0.013, Fig. 2H)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r8",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "anti-dsDNA 3.14 (2.13, 4.63) 5.28 (3.56, 7.82) 4.22 (2.85, 6.25) 3.06 (2.11, 4.44) 4.11 (2.80, 6.06)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r9",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Combined IL-6, anti-Ro/SSA, IL-5, ANA, MIG 0.93 (0.87, 0.97) 0.89 (0.77, 0.96) 0.96 (0.90, 0.99) 0.84(0.71, 0.93) 92% ± 1.78%",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r10",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "However, ANA negative, IL-5 and IFN-γ high cases (SLE cluster 1) were more likely to develop nephritis (p = 0.008), while cases who were ANA positive were more likely to develop arthritis (p = 0.028)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r11",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Cases who later developed SLE exhibited increased inflammatory mediators from multiple immune pathways more than 3.5 years pre-classification (Fig. 1 and Table 1).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r12",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Cases moving toward SLE classification gained an average of 0.5 dysregulated mediators per year, compared to only 0.06 in controls (p < 0.001; Fig. 2A and Table 2).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r13",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Of note, multiple TNF superfamily members, including TNFRI, TNFRII, BLyS, and APRIL, were dysregulated only as patients approached SLE classification (Fig. 1 and Table 1).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r14",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The detection of most lupus-associated autoantibody specificities occurred significantly later than the onset of IL-4, IL-5, IL-6, IFN-γ, or MIG dysregulation (Fig. 3 and Table 3).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r15",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Over the entire pre-classification period, random forest models incorporating ANA and anti-Ro/SSA positivity with levels of IL-5, IL-6, and the IFN-γ-induced chemokine, MIG, distinguished future SLE patients with 92% (±1.8%) accuracy",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r16",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "However, ANA negative, IL-5 and IFN-γ high cases (SLE cluster 1) were more likely to develop nephritis (p = 0.008), while cases who were ANA positive were more likely to develop arthritis (p = 0.028)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r17",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Indeed, these two mediators were elevated in about 20% of future SLE patients at least 6 years prior to disease transition and in approximately 90% of SLE patients by two years after classification.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r18",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Thus, the early elevation of IFN-γ, followed by significant increases in BLyS and APRIL within one year of disease classification when SLE is imminent, supports the model that simultaneous dysregulation",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r19",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "To determine if other forms of immune dysregulation contribute to preclinical SLE pathogenesis, we measured SLE-associated autoantibodies and soluble mediators",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r20",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "To determine if other forms of immune dysregulation contribute to preclinical SLE pathogenesis",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r21",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "To determine if other forms of immune dysregulation contribute to preclinical SLE pathogenesis",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r22",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "To better understand the temporal relationship between soluble mediator dysregulation and autoantibody production, we next compared the timing",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r23",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The data presented above suggest that altered soluble mediators are detected years before patients reach SLE classification and may improve the prognostic accuracy of ANA positivity",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r24",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Our current findings suggest that dysregulation of these cytokines, particularly IL-5 (Th2-type) and IL-6 (Th2/17-type), may be an essential early step in SLE pathogenesis.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r25",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Thus, the early elevation of IFN-γ, followed by significant increases in BLyS and APRIL within one year of disease classification when SLE is imminent, supports the model",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r26",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Future prospective, longitudinal studies of individuals with autoantibody positivity ± immune dysregulation, prior to onset of clinical signs and symptoms, will be necessary to determine which autoimmune disease(s) are associated with particular dysregulat",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r27",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Although the cellular sources of dysregulated soluble mediators in preclinical SLE remain unknown and are the subject of future study",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r28",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Additional, future studies will be required to determine if dysregulation of signaling pathways that leads to aberrant cellular activation and secretion of inflammatory mediators is due to genetic, epigenetic, and/or environmental triggers",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaut.2016.06.001",
      "@type": [
