    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n20",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Evidence",
        "Evidence"
      ],
      "title": "Random forest model across entire pre-classification period: combined predictors (ANA, anti-Ro/SSA, IL-5, IL-6, MIG) achieved 92% accuracy (±1.78%), sensitivity 0.93, specificity 0.89, PPV 0.96, NPV …",
      "content": "Random forest model across entire pre-classification period: combined predictors (ANA, anti-Ro/SSA, IL-5, IL-6, MIG) achieved 92% accuracy (±1.78%), sensitivity 0.93, specificity 0.89, PPV 0.96, NPV 0.84; ANA-only model 78% accuracy (±2.42%).\n\nFrom Table 4 'ALL' time period. Ten independent pre-SLE datasets generated with replacement; final model consisted of predictors appearing in at least 5 of 10 best RF models. Average prediction accuracy calculated across the ten datasets.",
      "created": "2026-11-06T16:43:35.762Z",
      "modified": "2026-11-06T16:43:35.762Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n20",
      "sourceDocument": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaut.2016.06.001"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n21",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Evidence",
        "Evidence"
      ],
      "title": "ANA-negative, IL-5-high, IFN-γ-high pre-SLE cluster (SLE cluster 1) had significantly higher nephritis risk (p=0.008) at classification compared to ANA-positive cluster, which had higher arthritis ri…",
      "content": "ANA-negative, IL-5-high, IFN-γ-high pre-SLE cluster (SLE cluster 1) had significantly higher nephritis risk (p=0.008) at classification compared to ANA-positive cluster, which had higher arthritis risk (p=0.028).\n\nFrom multidimensional scaling of RF proximity matrix (Fig. 4). Clusters compared for sex, race, age, medication history, and individual ACR criteria using Fisher's exact test, chi-square, or unpaired t-test.",
      "created": "2026-11-06T16:43:35.762Z",
      "modified": "2026-11-06T16:43:35.762Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n21",
      "sourceDocument": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaut.2016.06.001"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n22",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Request",
        "Request"
      ],
      "title": "Conduct prospective longitudinal studies of individuals with autoantibody positivity ± immune dysregulation prior to clinical symptoms to determine which autoimmune diseases associate with particular…",
      "content": "Conduct prospective longitudinal studies of individuals with autoantibody positivity ± immune dysregulation prior to clinical symptoms to determine which autoimmune diseases associate with particular dysregulated immune pathways.\n\nThe paper states future prospective studies are needed to determine which autoimmune diseases are associated with particular dysregulated immune pathways present before/concurrent with particular autoantibody specificities or clinical rheumatic disease.",
      "created": "2026-11-06T16:43:35.762Z",
      "modified": "2026-11-06T16:43:35.762Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n22"
    },
    {
